## Example from Class
To use `fork()`, you need to include the `<unistd.h>` library. Here is how you use the return value to decide what the parent and child should do:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <unistd.h>

int main() {
    int pid = fork(); // The function creates the clone here

    if (pid == 0) {
        printf("I am the child process!\n");
    } else {
        printf("I am the parent process!\n");
    }

    return 0;
}
```

